#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"GitHub Actions でも同じ順に流す（`.github/workflows/ci.yml`）。試験は、試験ご"
"とに一時の DB を作る。workflow の `image` は、`Containerfile` を arm64 の "
"runner で build し、[image に入る物](release.md#image-に入る物) を確かめ"
"（`ci/check-image.sh`）、空の image の中で起きて置いて読めること・止める合図"
"で終わること・起こし直しても残ることを見る（`ci/smoke-image.sh`）。release "
"の workflow も、同じ 2 つを push の前に流す。workflow の `cli` は、release に"
"付ける CLI を macOS（arm64）の runner で、出す時と同じ script（`ci/build-"
"cli.sh`）で作り、binary の形・つながる library・版・秘密の走査を確かめ（`ci/"
"check-cli.sh`）、その binary を同じ commit のサーバーに向けて打つ。"
msgstr ""
"GitHub Actions runs the same steps in the same order (`.github/workflows/"
"ci.yml`). Each test creates its own temporary DB. The workflow's `image` "
"builds the `Containerfile` on an arm64 runner, verifies [What goes into the "
"image](release.md#what-goes-into-the-image) (`ci/check-image.sh`), and "
"checks that, inside the empty image, it starts and can store and read, that "
"it exits on the stop signal, and that data remains after a restart (`ci/"
"smoke-image.sh`). The release workflow also runs the same two before the "
"push. The workflow's `cli` builds the CLI attached to a release on a macOS "
"(arm64) runner with the same script used for publishing (`ci/build-cli.sh`), "
"verifies the binary's format, linked libraries, version, and the secret scan "
"(`ci/check-cli.sh`), and runs that binary against the server from the same "
"commit."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"API の形（URL・引数の名・JSON の欄）を変える時は、先に [API の仕様]"
"(api.md#api-の版を上げる時上げない時) の「API の版を上げる時・上げない時」を"
"見る。変えたら、skills の `tpm page`（`cli/src/commands/page.ts`）と、その偽"
"の置き場（`cli/test/helpers.ts` の `FakeStore`）も合わせて直す。skills の CI "
"が、この repo の決めた版に向けて、つなぎの試験を流す。"
msgstr ""
"Before changing the shape of an endpoint (URLs, parameter names, JSON "
"fields), first read \"When to bump the API version, and when not to\" in "
"[API specification](api.md#when-to-bump-the-api-version-and-when-not-to). "
"After changing it, also update `tpm page` in skills (`cli/src/commands/"
"page.ts`) and its fake page store (`FakeStore` in `cli/test/helpers.ts`) to "
"match. The CI in skills runs the integration tests against the version this "
"repo specifies."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**SQL を変えた時**: SQL は `query!` が build の時に `.sqlx/` と突き合わせる。"
"SQL か `migrations/` を変えたら、一時の DB を作って作り直し、commit する（忘"
"れると CI の `cargo sqlx prepare --check` が落ちる）。`sqlx-cli` の版は "
"workflow の `SQLX_CLI_VERSION` と合わせる。"
msgstr ""
"**When you change SQL**: `query!` checks SQL against `.sqlx/` at build time. "
"If you change SQL or `migrations/`, create a temporary DB, regenerate `.sqlx/"
"`, and commit it (if you forget, `cargo sqlx prepare --check` in CI fails). "
"Keep the `sqlx-cli` version in sync with `SQLX_CLI_VERSION` in the workflow."

#: src/development.md
msgid "sqlite://$PWD/target/dev.db"
msgstr "sqlite://$PWD/target/dev.db"

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**当てた移行の SQL は変えない**: 動いている DB が、当てた SQL の中身を覚えて"
"いる。表を変える時は `migrations/` に次の番号の file を足し、`tests/"
"migrations.rs` の一覧に 1 行足す（前からある行が変わると、試験が落ちる）。"
msgstr ""
"**Never change an applied migration**: A running DB remembers the contents "
"of the SQL that was applied. To change a table, add a file with the next "
"number to `migrations/` and add one line to the list in `tests/"
"migrations.rs` (if an existing line changes, the test fails)."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**版を上げる**: `Cargo.toml` の `[workspace.package]` の `version` を上げ"
"（サーバーと `crates/` の crate が同じ版になる。`Cargo.lock` も変わる）、"
"`CHANGELOG.md` に、API の版が変わったかを書く。"
msgstr ""
"**Bump the version**: Bump `version` under `[workspace.package]` in "
"`Cargo.toml` (the server and the crates in `crates/` get the same version; "
"`Cargo.lock` changes too), and note in `CHANGELOG.md` whether the API "
"version changed."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**crate を上げる**: `.cargo/config.toml` の `global-min-publish-age` が、公開"
"から 2 日たっていない版を選ばせない（Cargo 1.100 から）。上げる時は `cargo "
"update` → 試験 → PR。`cargo install` はこの決まりを見ないので、道具は版を書い"
"て入れる。"
msgstr ""
"**Update crates**: `global-min-publish-age` in `.cargo/config.toml` prevents "
"selecting versions published less than 2 days ago (since Cargo 1.100). To "
"update: `cargo update` → tests → PR. `cargo install` does not honor this "
"rule, so install tools with an explicit version."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**弱点と license の見張り**: workflow の `advisories` が `cargo deny check "
"advisories licenses`（設定は `deny.toml`）を、PR ごとと週に 1 度流す。"
"`deny.toml` に無い license の crate が入ると落ちる。"
msgstr ""
"**Vulnerability and license monitoring**: The workflow's `advisories` runs "
"`cargo deny check advisories licenses` (configured in `deny.toml`) on every "
"PR and once a week. It fails when a crate with a license not listed in "
"`deny.toml` comes in."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**workflow の action**: commit の SHA で固定する（tag は後から中身が替わりう"
"る）。"
msgstr ""
"**Workflow actions**: Pin them by commit SHA (the contents behind a tag can "
"be replaced later)."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**main を守る決まり**: GitHub の ruleset「main: CI が通らないと merge できな"
"い」（Settings → Rules → Rulesets）が、`main` への変更に、CI の `test`・"
"`image`・`advisories`・`docs`・`cli` の 5 つが通っていることを求める。PR は、"
"5 つが通るまで merge できない。repo の admin は、この決まりを bypass できるの"
"で、`main` への直の push は通る（GitHub の必須の check には「PR だけに効かせ"
"る」選び方が無いので、直の push を通すには bypass になる）。admin は、わざと"
"選べば（画面の bypass の印・`gh pr merge --admin`）PR も CI を通さずに merge "
"できてしまうので、使わない。workflow の job の名を変えたら、ruleset の check "
"の名も合わせて直す（合わないと、PR がいつまでも merge できない）。"
msgstr ""
"**Branch protection for main**: The GitHub ruleset \"main: cannot merge "
"unless CI passes\" (Settings → Rules → Rulesets) requires that the five CI "
"checks `test`, `image`, `advisories`, `docs`, and `cli` pass for changes to "
"`main`. A PR cannot be merged until all five pass. Repo admins can bypass "
"this rule, so direct pushes to `main` go through (GitHub's required checks "
"have no option to \"apply to PRs only\", so allowing direct pushes means a "
"bypass). An admin who deliberately chooses to (the bypass checkbox in the "
"UI, or `gh pr merge --admin`) can also merge a PR without CI passing, so do "
"not use it. If you rename a workflow job, also update the check name in the "
"ruleset to match (otherwise PRs can never be merged)."

#: src/development.md
msgid "一覧の UI の試験"
msgstr "List UI tests"

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"一覧の UI は、HTML の字を `tests/ui.rs` が見て、browser でしか見えない物"
"（script の動き・色・幅での並び）を `e2e/` の試験が見る。`e2e/` は "
"[Playwright](https://playwright.dev/) の試験（TypeScript）で、同じ commit の "
"`pagetray-server` を一時の DB で起こし、本物の browser（Chromium）で開く。"
"Node が要るのはこの folder の中だけで、image にも CLI にも入らない。"
msgstr ""
"For the list UI, `tests/ui.rs` checks the text of the HTML, and the tests in "
"`e2e/` check what can only be seen in a browser (what the script does, "
"colors, and the layout at each width). `e2e/` holds [Playwright](https://"
"playwright.dev/) tests (TypeScript): they start the `pagetray-server` of the "
"same commit with a temporary DB and open it in a real browser (Chromium). "
"Node is needed only inside this folder, and it goes into neither the image "
"nor the CLI."

#: src/development.md
msgid "# 初めの 1 度だけ。試験用の Chromium を入れる\n"
msgstr "# Only the first time. Installs the Chromium used by the tests\n"

#: src/development.md
msgid "chrome"
msgstr "chrome"

#: src/development.md
msgid "# この機械の Chrome を使う（Chromium を入れなくてよい）\n"
msgstr ""
"# Use the Chrome installed on this machine (no need to install Chromium)\n"

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**CI**: workflow の `ui` が PR ごとに流す。落ちると、画面の絵と操作の記録が "
"artifact（`ui-report`）に残る。`ui` は、main を守る決まりの必須の check に、"
"まだ入れていない（時々落ちないことを見てから足す）。"
msgstr ""
"**CI**: The workflow's `ui` job runs them on every PR. When a test fails, a "
"screenshot and a trace of the steps are kept in the artifact (`ui-report`). "
"`ui` is not yet one of the required checks of the rule protecting main (it "
"will be added once it has been seen not to fail intermittently)."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**読むだけの試験**: 題に `@smoke` が付いた試験（`e2e/tests/smoke.spec.ts`）"
"は、何も置かず、何が置かれていても通る物だけを見る。`PAGETRAY_E2E_URL=http://"
"127.0.0.1:8801 pnpm test` と打つと、サーバーを起こさず、動いている置き場に向"
"けて、この試験だけが流れる（置く試験は、設定が流させない）。版を上げた後の確"
"かめに使う（[動かす](run.md#確かめる) の「確かめる」）。"
msgstr ""
"**Read-only test**: The test with `@smoke` in its title (`e2e/tests/"
"smoke.spec.ts`) puts nothing and checks only things that hold whatever is in "
"the store. With `PAGETRAY_E2E_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8801 pnpm test`, no "
"server is started and only this test runs, against the running store (the "
"configuration does not let the tests that put pages run). It is used to "
"verify after raising the version (\"Verify\" in [Running](run.md#verify))."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**試験を足す**: `e2e/tests/` に `*.spec.ts` を足す。ページは `helpers.ts` の "
"`place` で置き、区画（操作の帯・絞り込みの列・一覧の列・本文の枠）は "
"`helpers.ts` の関数で選ぶ。試験は同じ置き場に 1 本ずつ順に流れるので、試験ご"
"とに別の project の名を使う。新着の印を見る試験は、`openLive` で開いてから置"
"く（知らせにつながる前に置いたページの知らせは届かない）。大きな file は試験"
"の中で作り、repo に置かない。"
msgstr ""
"**Adding tests**: Add a `*.spec.ts` under `e2e/tests/`. Put pages with "
"`place` from `helpers.ts`, and select the regions (toolbar, filters, list, "
"viewer) with the functions in `helpers.ts`. The tests run one at a time "
"against the same store, so use a different project name in each test. A test "
"that looks at the new-page badge opens the UI with `openLive` before putting "
"a page (the notice for a page put before the connection is made never "
"arrives). Create large files inside the test; do not put them in the repo."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**template を変えた時**: `templates/index.html` を変えたら、この試験も流す。"
"試験が選ぶ手がかり（区画の id の `toolbar`・`filters`・`list`・`viewer`、"
"`#fresh`、`li[data-path]`、絞り込みの列の見出しの字など）を変える時は、同じ "
"PR で `helpers.ts` も直す。"
msgstr ""
"**When you change the template**: After changing `templates/index.html`, run "
"these tests too. When you change something the tests select by (the region "
"ids `toolbar`, `filters`, `list`, and `viewer`, `#fresh`, `li[data-path]`, "
"the heading text of the filters, and so on), fix `helpers.ts` in the same PR."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**Node の依存**: 依存は `@playwright/test` の 1 つで、版は `package.json` に"
"そのまま書く（`^` を付けない）。`pnpm-lock.yaml` を commit し、CI は `--"
"frozen-lockfile` で入れる。`pnpm-workspace.yaml` の `minimumReleaseAge` が、"
"公開から 2 日たっていない版を入れさせない。弱点は、workflow の `advisories` "
"が `pnpm audit` で、PR ごとと週に 1 度見る。版は手で上げる（Playwright を上げ"
"ると browser も替わるので、試験が通るのを見る）。`package.json` の版を書き替"
"え、`pnpm install` → 試験 → PR。"
msgstr ""
"**Node dependencies**: There is one dependency, `@playwright/test`, and its "
"version is written exactly in `package.json` (no `^`). `pnpm-lock.yaml` is "
"committed, and CI installs with `--frozen-lockfile`. `minimumReleaseAge` in "
"`pnpm-workspace.yaml` keeps out versions published less than 2 days ago. For "
"vulnerabilities, the workflow's `advisories` job runs `pnpm audit` on every "
"PR and once a week. Versions are raised by hand (raising Playwright also "
"changes the browser, so watch the tests pass): rewrite the version in "
"`package.json`, then `pnpm install` → tests → PR."

#: src/development.md
msgid "この本を直す"
msgstr "Editing this book"

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"この本は [mdBook](https://rust-lang.github.io/mdBook/) で作り、release の tag"
"（`v*`）を打った時に、workflow（`.github/workflows/docs.yml`）が GitHub "
"Pages に出す。PR と main への push では、build できるか・英語の訳が原文と合っ"
"ているか・作った本が browser で動くか（下の「本の試験」）を見る（job の名は "
"`docs`）。"
msgstr ""
"This book is built with [mdBook](https://rust-lang.github.io/mdBook/), and "
"the workflow (`.github/workflows/docs.yml`) publishes it to GitHub Pages "
"when a release tag (`v*`) is pushed. On PRs and pushes to main, it checks "
"that the book builds, that the English translation matches the source text, "
"and that the built book works in a browser (\"Book tests\" below); the job "
"is named `docs`."

#: src/development.md
msgid "`docs/book.toml`"
msgstr "`docs/book.toml`"

#: src/development.md
msgid "本の設定。組み込みの検索は切ってある（日本語が引けないため）"
msgstr ""
"The book's configuration. The built-in search is turned off (because it "
"cannot search Japanese)"

#: src/development.md
msgid "`docs/src/`"
msgstr "`docs/src/`"

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"原文（日本語）。目次は `SUMMARY.md`。語の決まりは `glossary.md`（用語集）"
msgstr ""
"The source text (Japanese). The table of contents is `SUMMARY.md`. The rules "
"for terms are in `glossary.md` (the Glossary)"

#: src/development.md
msgid "`docs/po/en.po`"
msgstr "`docs/po/en.po`"

#: src/development.md
msgid "英語の訳。原文の段落・表の升・コードの塊ごとに 1 項"
msgstr ""
"The English translation. One entry per paragraph, table cell, or code block "
"of the source text"

#: src/development.md
msgid "`docs/theme/site.js`・`site.css`"
msgstr "`docs/theme/site.js`, `site.css`"

#: src/development.md
msgid "上の帯に足す、言葉の切り替えと検索の枠"
msgstr "The language switcher and the search box added to the menu bar"

#: src/development.md
msgid "`docs/pagefind.yml`"
msgstr "`docs/pagefind.yml`"

#: src/development.md
msgid "検索（[Pagefind](https://pagefind.app/)）の索引に入れる物"
msgstr "What goes into the search ([Pagefind](https://pagefind.app/)) index"

#: src/development.md
msgid "`docs/mermaid.min.js`・`mermaid-init.js`"
msgstr "`docs/mermaid.min.js`, `mermaid-init.js`"

#: src/development.md
msgid "図（Mermaid）を描く script。`mdbook-mermaid install docs` が置いた物"
msgstr ""
"Scripts that render diagrams (Mermaid). Placed by `mdbook-mermaid install "
"docs`"

#: src/development.md
msgid "`ci/docs-po.sh`"
msgstr "`ci/docs-po.sh`"

#: src/development.md
msgid "`en.po` を原文に合わせる。`--check` を付けると、合っているかを見るだけ"
msgstr ""
"Syncs `en.po` with the source text. With `--check`, it only verifies that "
"they match"

#: src/development.md
msgid "`ci/docs-build.sh`"
msgstr "`ci/docs-build.sh`"

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"日本語の本を `docs/book/` に、英語の本を `docs/book/en/` に作り、検索の索引"
"を `docs/book/pagefind/` に作る"
msgstr ""
"Builds the Japanese book into `docs/book/`, the English book into `docs/book/"
"en/`, and the search index into `docs/book/pagefind/`"

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"道具は、workflow の `env` に書いた版を入れる（上げる時は、workflow の版と "
"checksum を一緒に上げる）。"
msgstr ""
"Install the tools at the versions written in the workflow's `env` (when "
"updating, bump the version and the checksum in the workflow together)."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"`ci/docs-build.sh` が本を `docs/book/` に作る。最後の行で配り、`http://"
"localhost:8000/` で見る。"
msgstr ""
"`ci/docs-build.sh` builds the book into `docs/book/`. The last line serves "
"it; open `http://localhost:8000/` to view it."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**mdbook-i18n-helpers は commit を名指して入れる**: 公開済みの 0.4.0 は、訳し"
"た本で囲み（`> [!WARNING]` など）を崩す。直し（[\\#344](https://github.com/"
"google/mdbook-i18n-helpers/pull/344)）を含む版が出たら、版の名指しに替える。"
msgstr ""
"**mdbook-i18n-helpers is installed by pinning a commit**: The published "
"0.4.0 breaks admonitions (`> [!WARNING]` and the like) in the translated "
"book. Once a version containing the fix ([\\#344](https://github.com/google/"
"mdbook-i18n-helpers/pull/344)) is released, switch to pinning a version."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**原文を直したら、同じ PR で英語も直す**: `ci/docs-po.sh` を流すと、足した段"
"落が `docs/po/en.po` に空の訳で入り、変えた段落に `#, fuzzy` の印が付く。空の"
"所と印の所を訳し、印の行を消す。`ci/docs-po.sh --check` が通れば済み（CI も同"
"じ検査を流す。原文にあって訳に無い段落・`fuzzy` の残り・訳に残った日本語があ"
"ると落ちる）。"
msgstr ""
"**When you edit the source text, update the English in the same PR**: "
"running `ci/docs-po.sh` adds new paragraphs to `docs/po/en.po` with an empty "
"translation and marks changed paragraphs with `#, fuzzy`. Translate the "
"empty and marked entries, and delete the marker lines. You are done when `ci/"
"docs-po.sh --check` passes (CI runs the same check; it fails on a source "
"paragraph with no translation, a leftover `fuzzy` marker, or Japanese left "
"in a translation)."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**コードの塊**: 訳に出るのは、コードの中の註（`#` の行）と、引用符の中の字だ"
"け。命令の中の置き換えの名は訳せないので、`<version>` のように英字で書く。行"
"の後ろに付けた註は、取り出されないことがある（`ci/docs-build.sh` が、英語の本"
"に日本語が残っていれば落ちる）。"
msgstr ""
"**Code blocks**: only comments (lines starting with `#`) and text inside "
"quotes are extracted for translation. Placeholders inside commands cannot be "
"translated, so write them in ASCII, such as `<version>`. A comment at the "
"end of a command line is sometimes not extracted (`ci/docs-build.sh` fails "
"if Japanese is left in the English book)."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**訳さない物も `msgstr` に書く**: 命令・URL だけの項は、原文をそのまま写す。"
"link の先の file の名（`run.md` など）は変えない。見出しを指す `#…` は、英語"
"の本では見出しの id が訳した題から作られるので、訳した見出しの id に書き替え"
"る（`release.md#image-に入る物` → `release.md#what-goes-into-the-image`）。"
msgstr ""
"**Fill in `msgstr` even for entries you do not translate**: for command-only "
"and URL-only entries, copy the source text as is. Do not change the file "
"name of a link target (such as `run.md`). For a `#…` that points to a "
"heading, rewrite it to the id of the translated heading, because in the "
"English book heading ids are generated from the translated titles (for "
"example, the link to the \"What goes into the image\" section becomes "
"`release.md#what-goes-into-the-image`)."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**語を足す・替える**: 先に [用語集](glossary.md) を直し、文書・註・code の名"
"をそれに合わせる。用語集に書いた id が画面に在るか・「使わない言い方」が戻っ"
"ていないかは、試験（`tests/terms.rs`）が見る。"
msgstr ""
"**Adding or changing a term**: First fix the [Glossary](glossary.md), then "
"make the documents, comments, and names in the code match it. A test (`tests/"
"terms.rs`) checks that the ids written in the glossary exist in the UI and "
"that the \"terms to avoid\" have not come back."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**章を足す**: `docs/src/` に file を置き、`SUMMARY.md` に 1 行足す。CLI の章"
"は `docs/src/cli.md`（「使う」の節の、動かす と API の仕様 の間）。"
msgstr ""
"**Add a chapter**: Put a file in `docs/src/` and add one line to "
"`SUMMARY.md`. The CLI chapter is `docs/src/cli.md` (in the \"Usage\" "
"section, between Running and API specification)."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**repo の file を指す link**: 本の外の file（`CHANGELOG.md` など）は、GitHub "
"の URL で書く。章どうしは、`run.md` のように file の名で書く。"
msgstr ""
"**Links to files in the repo**: For files outside the book (such as "
"`CHANGELOG.md`), use the GitHub URL. Between chapters, use the file name, as "
"in `run.md`."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**本の試験**: `e2e/docs-tests/` の試験（Playwright）が、作った本を本物の "
"browser で開き、どの章も開いて console に誤りが無いこと・図が描けること・検索"
"の枠が開いて日本語と英語の語が当たること・言葉の切り替えで同じ章へ移ることを"
"見る。`ci/docs-build.sh` の後に、`e2e/` で `pnpm test:docs` を打つ（道具の入"
"れ方は上の「一覧の UI の試験」と同じ）。CI では job `docs` が流す。章を足した"
"ら、`e2e/docs-tests/docs.spec.ts` の章の一覧にも足す（目次と合わないと落ち"
"る）。"
msgstr ""
"**Book tests**: The tests in `e2e/docs-tests/` (Playwright) open the built "
"book in a real browser and check that every chapter opens with no errors in "
"the console, that the diagrams render, that the search box opens and finds "
"Japanese and English words, and that the language switcher moves to the same "
"chapter. After `ci/docs-build.sh`, run `pnpm test:docs` in `e2e/` (the tools "
"are installed the same way as in \"List UI tests\" above). In CI, the `docs` "
"job runs them. When you add a chapter, also add it to the chapter list in "
"`e2e/docs-tests/docs.spec.ts` (the test fails if it does not match the table "
"of contents)."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**図**: ```` ```mermaid ```` の塊で書く。構文を間違えても build は通る。描け"
"るかは、本の試験が見る。"
msgstr ""
"**Diagrams**: Write them in ```` ```mermaid ```` blocks. The build passes "
"even if the syntax is wrong. The book tests check that they render."

#: src/development.md
msgid ""
"**検索と言葉の切り替え**: `docs/theme/site.js` は、mdBook の画面の `#mdbook-"
"menu-bar` と `path_to_root` に頼っている。mdBook を上げても検索の枠が開くこ"
"と・言葉が切り替わることは、本の試験が見る。"
msgstr ""
"**Search and the language switcher**: `docs/theme/site.js` depends on "
"`#mdbook-menu-bar` and `path_to_root` in mdBook's page. The book tests check "
"that the search box still opens and that the language still switches after "
"mdBook is updated."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"pagetray の文書・画面・code で使う語を、1 か所に並べる。語を足す・替える時"
"は、先にここを直し、文書と code をそれに合わせる。"
msgstr ""
"The terms used in pagetray's documents, UI, and code are listed here in one "
"place. When adding or changing a term, fix this page first, then make the "
"documents and the code match it."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid "**語**: 文書で使う語。かっこの中は、英語の本と code で使う語。"
msgstr "**Term**: The term used in the documents and in the code."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"**code の名**: HTML の id（`#…`）・class（`.…`）・型・欄・命令など。無ければ"
"「—」。"
msgstr ""
"**Name in code**: An HTML id (`#…`), a class (`.…`), a type, a field, a "
"command, and so on. \"—\" if there is none."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"**使わない言い方**: 前に使っていた語や、ほかの物と紛れる語。文書にも註にも書"
"かない。"
msgstr ""
"**Terms to avoid**: Terms used earlier, or terms that can be confused with "
"something else. They are not written in documents or comments."

#: src/glossary.md
msgid ""
"[skills](https://github.com/uraitakahito/skills) の `tpm` の語（担当・依頼"
"書・控えなど）は、skills の docs にある。"
msgstr ""
"The terms of `tpm` in [skills](https://github.com/uraitakahito/skills) "
"(roles, briefs, local copies, and so on) are in the skills docs."

